  "properties": {
    "title": "Canopy height: 2019-2020",
    "description": "Tree canopy height map for India built by [ACT4D](http://act4d.iitd.ernet.in/) research group at [IIT Delhi](https://home.iitd.ac.in/). Tree canopy height layer describes how tall are trees in a given pixel. \nThe Pan India map (except ACZ 12-15)  is available from 2017 onwards at 25m resolution.\nThese are the classes in the current version of the map: \n\n1.Short \n2.Medium\n3.Tall \n\nDetails of methodology can be found  in the [technical manual](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZxovdpPThkN09cB1TcUYSE2BImI7M3k_/view) and the codebase at https://github.com/Dhruvi-Goyal/Tree-Health-Monitoring/",
